1
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:07,080
Why do you seem so busy all the time lately?

2
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:08,400
Working late into the night.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:09,800
Didn't I tell you before?

4
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:12,080
Don't be too emotional.

5
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:13,840
Jennalee

6
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:15,960
is my personal secretary

7
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:18,000
If anyone gives him other work to do again,

8
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:19,760
it's equivalent to messing with my person

9
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:21,800
without permission.

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,960
I'm sorry for misunderstanding you about Put.

11
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,640
Can you forgive me, P'Jane?

12
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:32,119
Have you ever trusted me?

13
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:34,160
Are you still angry with me about that, P'Jane?

14
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,640
I'm not angry with you,

15
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:37,040
I'm angry at myself

16
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:39,080
for making it impossible for you to trust me.

17
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:41,040
Can we start over again?

18
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:41,760
P'Jane!

19
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:42,480
P'Jane!

20
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:43,200
P'Jane!

21
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:44,480
Oh!

22
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:46,480
Oh!

23
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:13,600
Are you ok?

24
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:17,800
I'm fine.

25
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:21,200
I'm so sorry, P'Jane.

26
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:24,600
P'Jane...

27
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:25,600
P'Jane...

28
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:09,080
You walk in with a warning sign

29
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:16,440
Just one look and already falling for you

30
00:02:19,079 --> 00:02:24,040
My friends tell me not to cross that line

31
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:31,000
But I’m already out of time

32
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:35,160
I know the truth, I taste the sin

33
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:36,800
It’s wrong but I don’t want it to be true

34
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,320
I’m losing all my discipline

35
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:43,480
You’re all I’m thinking of

36
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:45,480
and I’m breaking all the rules

37
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:47,760
just because…

38
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:51,120
You’re a red flag but I’m colorblind

39
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:54,640
I know you’re dangerous

40
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:58,240
If it burns, let it burn me alive

41
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:03,040
I can't hold myself back, I’d cross every line

42
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:10,280
Ooh

43
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,680
Hi, JP!

44
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:38,079
Haven't seen you in a long time,

45
00:03:38,079 --> 00:03:38,920
you little rascal.

46
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:41,440
How was your flight?

47
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:43,800
I've has never flown on a plane

48
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:45,280
alone this far before.

49
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:48,280
But the staff took really good care of me!

50
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:50,280
Well, that's not surprising.

51
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:52,000
You flew first class.

52
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:54,160
That was Daddy's idea.

53
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,560
I didn't pick it, you know.

54
00:03:58,079 --> 00:03:58,680
Oh!

55
00:03:59,079 --> 00:03:59,880
Auntie May!

56
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:02,000
You still remember me?

57
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:03,360
The last time we met,

58
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:05,240
you were still so very young!

59
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:06,400
Of course!

60
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:07,280
I remember!

61
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:08,840
The last time I came to Thailand,

62
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:11,160
Auntie May was with me all the time.

63
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:13,320
And you spent more time with me

64
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:14,880
than JP

65
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,040
and Daddy combined, probably!

66
00:04:18,079 --> 00:04:19,120
Coming to Thailand this time,

67
00:04:19,839 --> 00:04:21,079
promise me, okay?

68
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:23,280
You have to take me to travel around Thailand!

69
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:25,040
Don't ignore me like last time!

70
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,280
Of course.

71
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:29,280
Later, I'll take you to eat lots of delicious food.

72
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:32,440
You promised, okay?

73
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:41,360
Whoa!!

74
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:18,760
Is something up, P'Jane?

75
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:20,160
Well, I'm going to assign you work.

76
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:22,880
Am I not allowed to, Mr. Secretary?

77
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:29,760
Of course you can.

78
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:31,280
Go ahead and assign it.

79
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:33,480
Could you help me find a nanny?

80
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:36,960
A nanny?

81
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,520
Don't tell me...

82
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:45,200
you have a kid, P'Jane?

83
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:49,640
A boy named Jamie,

84
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,600
he's twelve-year-old .

85
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,560
He's half-American.

86
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:55,080
He just moved to Thailand.

87
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:59,040
I've already handled the school arrangements.

88
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:00,560
Right now, I want someone to

89
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:01,680
drop him off and pick him up,

90
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:03,080
take him out to travel,

91
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:04,680
and find things for him to do.

92
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,160
Understood.

93
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:13,960
I'll try contacting a nanny agency for you.

94
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:19,840
Jane.

95
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,080
Are you free this evening after work?

96
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,280
Uh...

97
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:30,600
yes, I'm free.

98
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,120
Is something up, P'Jane?

99
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:37,560
Want to go have dinner together?

100
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:39,840
Huh?

101
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:21,880
Mm.

102
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,560
I'm ready, JP!

103
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:28,960
What should we go eat?

104
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:30,280
Hello.

105
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:30,880
Hello.

106
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,520
And...

107
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,280
who's this?

108
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:36,600
My name is Little Jane.

109
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:37,720
Jane!?

110
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:40,200
Then that's the same name as JP!

111
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:45,360
He calls me JP,

112
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,920
short for my full name, Jane Patrick.

113
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:50,480
Why...

114
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,640
don't you call him father or daddy?

115
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:02,400
Oh.

116
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:04,000
JP,

117
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:06,640
why did you trick him?

118
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:07,640
Yeah,

119
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:10,160
JP isn't my daddy.

120
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:13,520
I'm JP's younger brother.

121
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:15,360
I didn't trick him.

122
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:17,440
He came to that conclusion all on his own.

123
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:24,520
Ah, then what should we do?

124
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:26,360
You have the exact same name as JP,

125
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:27,560
how should we call you

126
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,600
without getting confused?

127
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:30,120
Then,

128
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:31,640
how about this?

129
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:33,600
Back in university,

130
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:35,280
everyone called me Little Jane.

131
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:37,600
So how about you call me

132
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:39,080
P'Little Jane?

133
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:41,880
Lek means little.

134
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:43,840
Then..

135
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:45,680
Can I can you Lil' Jane?

136
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:48,040
Jamie...

137
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:50,000
you gave me a name like

138
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:51,640
a rapper!

139
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:55,600
Yo, my name is Lil' Jane!

140
00:08:59,400 --> 00:08:59,880
Come on,

141
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:00,720
let's get going.

142
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:03,520
I've already booked a table at a restaurant.

143
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:15,400
What do you and Jamie want to eat?

144
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,480
I can eat anything.

145
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:21,960
It's up to you, P'Jane.

146
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:23,840
I want to eat Pad Thai.

147
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:26,440
I heard that when you come to Thailand,

148
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,720
you have to eat Pad Thai.

149
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:29,920
No way.

150
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:31,880
Pad Thai has peanuts in it.

151
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,280
Are you allergic to peanuts, Jamie?

152
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:39,440
Yeah.

153
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:41,200
If I eat them, I can't breathe,

154
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:42,600
so I always have to carry

155
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:45,600
allergy medicine with me.

156
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:47,760
I'll keep that in mind

157
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:49,880
in case I buy snacks for you.

158
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:51,680
Sure, come over often!

159
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:53,640
Come and play with me.

160
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:55,360
I feel so lonely at home,

161
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:56,720
I don't really have any friends.

162
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:09,320
It's so pretty!

163
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:10,800
I want it!

164
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:11,880
Go ahead.

165
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:13,280
I'll buy it for you.

166
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:16,920
No, JP.

167
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:19,200
I want the real one.

168
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,000
Do you even know how to drive?

169
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,480
Wait until you're older, you little rascal.

170
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:26,760
Hmm.

171
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:31,600
Do you like race cars, Jamie?

172
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:32,320
Yeah!

173
00:10:32,680 --> 00:10:34,240
I like cars that go fast.

174
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:35,280
When I grow up,

175
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:38,280
I'm gonna be a Formula One race car driver!

176
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:44,280
Someone like you can definitely do it for sure!

177
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:51,600
You're going down!

178
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:52,800
Whoa!

179
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:54,640
Oh wow!

180
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:55,440
Oh wow!

181
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:56,280
Oh wow!

182
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,240
How did you get over five thousand points?!

183
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:10,600
I'm not giving up!

184
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:12,000
Me neither!

185
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,120
Over five thousand points!

186
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:30,840
Yay!

187
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:55,520
Oh wow!

188
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:13,280
Yes!

189
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:14,200
Whoa,

190
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:16,600
you're so good, Jamie!

191
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:17,600
I lost again.

192
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:19,800
Let me play another game, Lil' Jane!

193
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:20,880
No way.

194
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:24,000
I'll go wait over there with JP.

195
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:31,720
P'Jane, aren't you going to try playing

196
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:32,640
with Jamie?

197
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:34,760
I don't really like playing these kinds of things.

198
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,240
What about the person I asked you to

199
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:40,760
find to take care of Jamie?

200
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:44,040
I've checked both on websites and

201
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:46,280
called nanny placement agencies,

202
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:47,960
but none of them match the qualifications

203
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:49,200
you're looking for yet.

204
00:12:50,280 --> 00:12:50,800
But

205
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:52,200
I'll hurry and look for one for you.

206
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:00,360
I think there's no need now.

207
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:02,280
I found one.

208
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:10,400
Jamie seems to really like you, Jane.

209
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:12,880
What do you think

210
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:15,800
if I have you be Jamie's nanny

211
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:17,080
outside of company work hours?

212
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:21,680
Do you want to do it, Jane?

213
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:26,480
Sure!

214
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:29,200
I'll take the best care of Jamie!

215
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:32,520
And...

216
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:34,840
do you want to stay at my place, Jane?

217
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:42,400
So it's convenient to take care of Jamie.

218
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:52,120
Yeah.

219
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:54,120
Come stay at my house.

220
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:56,760
Come live together with me and JP.

221
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,800
JP also wants to be close to Lil' Jane too.

222
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:02,080
I know.

223
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:03,280
I can tell.

224
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:07,600
Watch it, you little rascal.

225
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:46,840
It's so wonderful.

226
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:47,880
Now that there's someone

227
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:49,040
else staying in this house,

228
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:51,960
so Mr.Jane won't be lonely anymore.

229
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:54,640
Mm.

230
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:55,960
Let me help carry that for you. Oh,

231
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:57,000
it's alright.

232
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:57,640
Oh, okay.

233
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:58,880
Then make yourself at home.

234
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,080
I'll take my leave now.

235
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:01,320
Thank you.

236
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:01,920
Sure.

237
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,320
Follow me.

238
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:08,280
I'll show you around the house.

239
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:40,800
You are strictly forbidden

240
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:41,560
from entering that room.

241
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:43,080
It's a restricted area.

242
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:45,880
A restricted area?

243
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:47,200
Everyone is forbidden

244
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,200
from entering that room.

245
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:50,800
It's my private office.

246
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:28,480
This is your room, Jane.

247
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:32,760
The room is so spacious.

248
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:35,080
And...

249
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:37,680
the bed looks so soft and comfortable too!

250
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:42,840
So, do you like it, Jane?

251
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:49,800
I love it.

252
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:56,960
And...

253
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:00,720
I'm happy

254
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:03,880
that I get to know your world better, P'Jane.

255
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:23,720
It really is soft.

256
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:52,520
You’re a red flag but I’m colorblind

257
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:55,960
I know you’re dangerous

258
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:59,760
If it burns, let it burn me alive

259
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:03,640
I can't hold myself back, I’d cross every line

260
00:18:03,640 --> 00:18:07,040
You’re a red flag but I’m colorblind

261
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:10,520
I’d give up anything for you

262
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:14,160
Even if it burns, I'm willing to melt away

263
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:19,320
I can't hold myself back, I’d cross every line

264
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:27,440
Uh...

265
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:31,360
I'm sorry.

266
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:38,800
I forgot.

267
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:52,400
This is what Jamie needs to do,

268
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,440
which is your schedule, Jane.

269
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,440
Drop off and pick up at the international school

270
00:18:58,440 --> 00:18:59,480
in the morning and evening,

271
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:00,480
and after that,

272
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:01,760
there are private tutoring sessions.

273
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:03,760
On Saturdays, there are piano lessons,

274
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:05,600
and going out every Sunday.

275
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:09,040
Jamie's schedule is so packed!

276
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:12,160
Just like your schedule.

277
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:19,640
Right?

278
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:20,320
Correct.

279
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:21,920
Very clever, Jamie.

280
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:24,920
Oh, right.

281
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:27,680
JP said that Lil' Jane

282
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:29,400
is really good at drawing cartoons.

283
00:19:37,120 --> 00:19:38,080
I'm sorry, Jamie.

284
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:41,280
I stopped drawing cartoons a long time ago.

285
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:43,680
I've probably forgotten it all.

286
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:45,880
Please, please, please?

287
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:47,480
Just a little bit is fine!

288
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:50,560
Alright then.

289
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:53,680
So

290
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:55,920
what do you want me to draw?

291
00:19:57,120 --> 00:19:58,200
How about drawing Jamie?

292
00:19:58,560 --> 00:19:59,640
Hmm...

293
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:05,160
It's better to draw a picture of JP!

294
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:14,840
Sure thing, Jamie.

295
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:16,760
I'll draw it for you, okay?

296
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:17,800
Mm.

297
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:24,440
Come on, Jamie.

298
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:26,480
First off,

299
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:29,200
we have to draw his outline first.

300
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:30,680
You're making that kind of face...

301
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:34,800
Are you drawing me as a demon again?

302
00:21:39,920 --> 00:21:41,000
Well, it's a demon

303
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:45,480
that is the most handsome.

304
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:57,200
Okay,

305
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:58,640
I'm done drawing.

306
00:21:59,000 --> 00:21:59,640
Whoa.

307
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:04,120
Lil' Jane draws so beautifully.

308
00:22:05,520 --> 00:22:06,800
Teach me.

309
00:22:07,480 --> 00:22:08,400
I...

310
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:10,120
want to draw a race car.

311
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:12,680
Sure.

312
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:15,360
You really love race cars, don't you, Jamie?

313
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:19,920
I like all sports that involve speed.

314
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:21,760
I even play the skateboard.

315
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:23,360
And I used to play football

316
00:22:23,360 --> 00:22:24,680
when I was in America too.

317
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:25,720
Really?

318
00:22:25,880 --> 00:22:26,400
Mm-hmm.

319
00:22:26,600 --> 00:22:27,800
I like playing football as well!

320
00:22:28,240 --> 00:22:28,720
Heh.

321
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:30,480
Let me know when you want to play together.

322
00:22:31,800 --> 00:22:32,480
Deal.

323
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:43,280
Jamie!

324
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:44,240
Wait for me!

325
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:48,960
Don't run in the dining room!

326
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:53,480
You'll end up bumping into something again!

327
00:22:58,560 --> 00:22:59,200
Jamie,

328
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:03,240
is P'Jane always

329
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:05,040
this bossy to everyone?

330
00:23:05,520 --> 00:23:06,040
Oh?

331
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:07,400
You get nagged by him too, Lil' Jane?

332
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,880
I thought I was the only one getting scolded!

333
00:23:23,320 --> 00:23:24,360
Hello, Jamie!

334
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:25,400
How are you doing?

335
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,080
How's Thailand treating you?

336
00:23:29,480 --> 00:23:30,840
It's super great, Daddy!

337
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,160
JP took me sightseeing

338
00:23:32,360 --> 00:23:34,480
and we ate so much delicious food!

339
00:23:34,840 --> 00:23:37,400
And tomorrow I'm going to a new school!

340
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:38,560
Have fun!

341
00:23:39,240 --> 00:23:41,000
When you first transfer to a new school,

342
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:42,640
you might not have many friends at first,

343
00:23:42,880 --> 00:23:44,120
but just do your best, okay?

344
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:45,400
It's okay.

345
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:47,640
I'm friendly with everyone anyway.

346
00:23:47,840 --> 00:23:48,360
Oh,

347
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:49,760
and right now,

348
00:23:51,360 --> 00:23:53,000
I have a new friend!

349
00:23:53,320 --> 00:23:53,880
Oh, really?

350
00:23:54,200 --> 00:23:54,920
Who is it?

351
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:57,000
He is

352
00:23:57,280 --> 00:23:58,280
my nanny.

353
00:23:58,600 --> 00:24:00,400
And he's JP's friend too.

354
00:24:00,960 --> 00:24:02,200
His name is also Jane.

355
00:24:02,280 --> 00:24:03,480
So I call him

356
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:04,560
Lil' Jane.

357
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:05,680
That's wonderful!

358
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:06,840
So you're not lonely anymore, right?

359
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,400
When can Daddy come visit me?

360
00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:11,400
Hmm...

361
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:12,080
things are

362
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:13,760
super busy right now, Jamie.

363
00:24:14,360 --> 00:24:14,880
In fact,

364
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:15,960
in just a bit,

365
00:24:16,360 --> 00:24:18,400
I have to fly out for a meeting in China.

366
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:19,760
That's all for now, okay?

367
00:24:19,880 --> 00:24:20,400
Mm.

368
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:22,280
In that case, have a safe trip.

369
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:25,080
Oh, do you want to talk to JP?

370
00:24:25,880 --> 00:24:26,360
It's fine.

371
00:24:26,560 --> 00:24:27,680
Daddy has to go now.

372
00:24:28,760 --> 00:24:29,240
Bye-bye.

373
00:24:51,040 --> 00:24:52,080
So in short,

374
00:24:52,960 --> 00:24:54,760
the number is two hundred, right?

375
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:56,200
Probably not.

376
00:24:56,480 --> 00:24:57,000
Huh?

377
00:24:57,520 --> 00:24:58,000
Oh.

378
00:24:58,760 --> 00:24:59,480
Aha.

379
00:24:59,640 --> 00:25:01,400
I must have received the wrong info then.

380
00:25:09,760 --> 00:25:10,240
Gap!

381
00:25:10,960 --> 00:25:11,480
Whoa,

382
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:12,520
gone already?

383
00:25:13,160 --> 00:25:14,080
Leaving early today, huh?

384
00:25:14,600 --> 00:25:15,680
I have another gig to get to.

385
00:25:17,080 --> 00:25:17,760
Good luck.

386
00:25:20,280 --> 00:25:22,560
Leaving in such a hurry, Jane!

387
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:24,000
Where are you rushing off to?

388
00:25:26,840 --> 00:25:27,480
Well, it's just that...

389
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:28,040
My goodness, Sis!

390
00:25:28,120 --> 00:25:29,280
You don't know?

391
00:25:29,880 --> 00:25:30,880
Right now,

392
00:25:30,880 --> 00:25:31,640
Jane has taken on the role of

393
00:25:31,640 --> 00:25:33,400
caring for the CEO's younger brother

394
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:34,680
as a side hustle!

395
00:25:35,120 --> 00:25:36,480
Ooh!

396
00:25:37,320 --> 00:25:38,880
That's just how it goes, isn't it?

397
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:40,720
When you've got connections

398
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:42,480
and you're close with the CEO,

399
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:45,000
you get way more privileges than everyone else!

400
00:25:45,400 --> 00:25:47,680
Getting to work in the same room,

401
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:51,280
and even getting to sleep at the same house

402
00:25:51,280 --> 00:25:53,280
with the boss!

403
00:25:53,280 --> 00:25:54,680
Eek!

404
00:25:54,680 --> 00:25:55,440
So fabulous, really!

405
00:25:55,440 --> 00:25:56,040
Fabulous, right?

406
00:25:56,040 --> 00:25:57,400
So fabulous!

407
00:25:57,400 --> 00:25:58,880
I wish I had that kind of luck!

408
00:25:58,880 --> 00:25:59,360
Yes,

409
00:26:00,080 --> 00:26:02,000
but I always complete my work to the end.

410
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:04,080
Is he dissing us?

411
00:26:04,880 --> 00:26:06,360
Jane, you...

412
00:26:06,560 --> 00:26:07,920
Don't mind people who spend their days

413
00:26:08,080 --> 00:26:09,200
snooping into other people's business

414
00:26:09,200 --> 00:26:10,320
instead of doing their own jobs.

415
00:26:10,680 --> 00:26:11,560
Hey, Gap!

416
00:26:11,720 --> 00:26:13,280
We are your seniors, you know!

417
00:26:14,760 --> 00:26:16,480
Then I apologize, my seniors.

418
00:26:17,280 --> 00:26:19,200
By the way, working like this,

419
00:26:19,520 --> 00:26:21,040
are you going to pass your KPIs this year?

420
00:26:21,040 --> 00:26:21,880
I'm worried!

421
00:26:21,880 --> 00:26:22,680
Gap!

422
00:26:23,680 --> 00:26:24,880
Honestly,

423
00:26:25,480 --> 00:26:26,840
stop messing with him.

424
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:28,840
Otherwise, I'll report you to Mr.Lilac.

425
00:26:30,800 --> 00:26:32,600
Jane might not be a snitch,

426
00:26:33,440 --> 00:26:35,800
but I am a massive snitch.

427
00:26:37,280 --> 00:26:38,280
We didn't even say anything!

428
00:26:39,280 --> 00:26:39,800
Mm.

429
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,680
I'm gonna hurry up with my work and rush out

430
00:26:44,400 --> 00:26:45,680
to watch a movie with Cherry too.

431
00:26:46,720 --> 00:26:47,680
You should hurry up and go,

432
00:26:48,200 --> 00:26:49,000
before you end up stuck here unable to go home

433
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:49,760
like certain people.

434
00:26:51,800 --> 00:26:52,880
Why are you still standing there? Go on!

435
00:26:52,880 --> 00:26:54,040
Okay, okay.

436
00:26:56,440 --> 00:26:57,600
Goodbye, seniors.

437
00:26:59,880 --> 00:27:01,280
Come on, Jamie.

438
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:04,360
Take the shot.

439
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:10,840
Is something wrong, Jamie?

440
00:27:12,080 --> 00:27:13,040
Why the long face?

441
00:27:13,320 --> 00:27:14,280
Hmm...

442
00:27:14,960 --> 00:27:17,000
I told you used to play football,

443
00:27:17,280 --> 00:27:18,840
not soccer.

444
00:27:23,960 --> 00:27:25,400
Did you mean

445
00:27:26,240 --> 00:27:27,480
American football?

446
00:27:27,840 --> 00:27:28,600
Yeah..

447
00:27:29,360 --> 00:27:30,000
It's okay.

448
00:27:30,280 --> 00:27:31,000
In that case,

449
00:27:31,880 --> 00:27:33,120
let me teach you.

450
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:34,440
Ok.

451
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:35,960
Look at the ball.

452
00:27:36,200 --> 00:27:37,520
We are going to look at.

453
00:27:37,520 --> 00:27:38,040
Uh huh.

454
00:27:38,080 --> 00:27:39,200
The goal we're kicking to.

455
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:39,720
Ok.

456
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:46,280
Hey?

457
00:27:46,360 --> 00:27:47,480
Why was it like that?

458
00:27:48,600 --> 00:27:49,280
Kick it over there.

459
00:27:49,720 --> 00:27:50,320
Careful.

460
00:28:00,400 --> 00:28:01,240
Jamie!

461
00:28:02,800 --> 00:28:03,880
You kicked the ball so hard.

462
00:29:03,480 --> 00:29:04,040
Hello?

463
00:29:09,800 --> 00:29:10,920
What do you want this time?

464
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:33,360
Thank you so much

465
00:29:33,760 --> 00:29:35,240
for giving me the time.

466
00:29:36,280 --> 00:29:37,280
Please cut to the chase.

467
00:29:38,920 --> 00:29:39,920
What do you want this time?

468
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:43,560
It's just that...

469
00:29:44,880 --> 00:29:46,320
For the upcoming civil servant transfer

470
00:29:46,320 --> 00:29:47,800
round this October,

471
00:29:49,280 --> 00:29:51,200
I would like to be promoted to Director-General.

472
00:29:52,280 --> 00:29:53,200
Mr.Jane,

473
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:55,400
is there any way you could help me out?

474
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:57,880
That is quite a difficult request.

475
00:29:59,200 --> 00:30:00,360
I do have some connections

476
00:30:00,360 --> 00:30:01,760
on the political side,

477
00:30:04,360 --> 00:30:05,160
however,

478
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:09,000
I wouldn't recommend asking for a favor

479
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:10,400
regarding a matter like this.

480
00:30:12,520 --> 00:30:14,120
The harder the favor,

481
00:30:15,800 --> 00:30:18,000
the higher the price of the exchange will be.

482
00:30:20,320 --> 00:30:22,040
Are you really willing to pay for it?

483
00:30:23,680 --> 00:30:24,240
Of course.

484
00:30:24,800 --> 00:30:25,920
If I get the position,

485
00:30:26,680 --> 00:30:28,200
I'm willing to pay whatever it takes.

486
00:30:59,800 --> 00:31:00,720
Thank you so much.

487
00:31:42,320 --> 00:31:43,280
Were you eavesdropping on my conversation

488
00:31:43,280 --> 00:31:44,280
with the client?

489
00:31:46,760 --> 00:31:47,360
A client?

490
00:31:48,800 --> 00:31:50,680
Or someone coming to ask for a favor?

491
00:31:54,960 --> 00:31:56,200
So you really were eavesdropping.

492
00:31:58,680 --> 00:32:00,280
Don't do this again next time.

493
00:32:02,040 --> 00:32:03,040
If it were someone else,

494
00:32:04,680 --> 00:32:06,120
you could end up in danger.

495
00:32:06,960 --> 00:32:08,200
Has your favor game...

496
00:32:09,280 --> 00:32:10,880
really come this far?

497
00:32:13,080 --> 00:32:13,840
I think it's better if you don't

498
00:32:13,840 --> 00:32:15,040
meddle in this matter.

499
00:32:19,800 --> 00:32:20,920
Don't you remember when you followed me

500
00:32:20,920 --> 00:32:22,560
to see how favors are done?

501
00:32:24,040 --> 00:32:24,560
Ouch!

502
00:32:28,960 --> 00:32:29,640
P'Jane!

503
00:32:34,440 --> 00:32:35,760
P'Jane, haven't you ever thought

504
00:32:36,720 --> 00:32:37,840
that you can't keep doing things

505
00:32:37,840 --> 00:32:39,400
like this forever?

506
00:32:40,800 --> 00:32:41,600
I know

507
00:32:42,120 --> 00:32:42,920
you're capable,

508
00:32:45,280 --> 00:32:47,280
but what if things go wrong like that day?

509
00:32:47,680 --> 00:32:49,280
You're not on your own anymore.

510
00:32:49,680 --> 00:32:50,320
You have...

511
00:32:57,320 --> 00:32:58,000
you have Jamie.

512
00:32:59,960 --> 00:33:00,800
And what if those who hold a grudge

513
00:33:00,800 --> 00:33:02,200
against you can't hurt you,

514
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:05,680
so they target the people around you instead?

515
00:33:13,120 --> 00:33:13,920
If that's the case,

516
00:33:15,960 --> 00:33:17,440
I'll protect everyone myself.

517
00:33:20,880 --> 00:33:22,680
I guess I can't force you to do anything.

518
00:33:25,880 --> 00:33:27,640
If there's ever a day you can't handle it anymore,

519
00:33:28,560 --> 00:33:29,800
just let me know.

520
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:45,360
(Thanapat Piboonosot)

521
00:33:45,360 --> 00:33:46,600
Honestly, Jane,

522
00:33:47,320 --> 00:33:48,480
working as an executive secretary

523
00:33:48,480 --> 00:33:49,920
was already good enough, son.

524
00:33:49,920 --> 00:33:51,440
Why resign just to become a nanny

525
00:33:51,840 --> 00:33:53,600
and make things hard on yourself?

526
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:55,720
It's not hard at all.

527
00:33:56,560 --> 00:33:58,280
Jamie is smart and easy to talk to.

528
00:33:59,240 --> 00:33:59,840
Whatever I teach him,

529
00:33:59,840 --> 00:34:01,000
he understands and can do it right away.

530
00:34:01,400 --> 00:34:01,880
Hmm...

531
00:34:03,760 --> 00:34:06,240
But isn't your boss working you a bit too hard?

532
00:34:06,360 --> 00:34:07,760
Oh, not at all.

533
00:34:08,199 --> 00:34:09,239
He's more than willing!

534
00:34:09,400 --> 00:34:10,679
Just getting to be close to Big Jane

535
00:34:10,679 --> 00:34:12,000
makes him happy enough!

536
00:34:14,239 --> 00:34:14,920
Uh...

537
00:34:15,080 --> 00:34:17,199
he even gave him a raise!

538
00:34:17,480 --> 00:34:19,560
An extra eighty thousand baht a month!

539
00:34:20,400 --> 00:34:21,800
Hmm? If it were me,

540
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:24,440
I could easily take care of ten more Jamies!

541
00:34:25,320 --> 00:34:26,040
Whoa!

542
00:34:26,520 --> 00:34:27,880
An extra eighty thousand?!

543
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:28,800
Eighty thousand!

544
00:34:30,280 --> 00:34:31,080
Jane,

545
00:34:31,800 --> 00:34:33,320
then you have to work hard

546
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:35,040
and stay dedicated, son,

547
00:34:36,400 --> 00:34:38,000
so you can save up and buy a car

548
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:39,600
for yourself to use.

549
00:34:39,600 --> 00:34:41,040
That way you won't have to share one

550
00:34:41,040 --> 00:34:42,280
with Jet and Jean all the time.

551
00:34:42,280 --> 00:34:42,800
Whoa,

552
00:34:43,080 --> 00:34:44,600
why did you change your mind so quickly?

553
00:34:44,960 --> 00:34:45,480
Why not?

554
00:34:46,480 --> 00:34:47,199
Is it a bad thing?

555
00:34:47,520 --> 00:34:48,159
Hmm...

556
00:34:48,280 --> 00:34:49,040
No, it's good!

557
00:34:49,040 --> 00:34:49,600
It's great!

558
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:50,199
Yeah.

559
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:51,520
Come on, let's go.

560
00:34:51,639 --> 00:34:52,239
Oh,

561
00:34:53,040 --> 00:34:53,639
Jet.

562
00:34:53,960 --> 00:34:55,000
Took you long enough to come down.

563
00:34:55,400 --> 00:34:56,080
Were you practicing dancing?

564
00:34:56,360 --> 00:34:57,160
Yeah, Bro.

565
00:34:57,720 --> 00:34:58,760
Preparing for an audition.

566
00:34:58,880 --> 00:35:00,720
Hmm. I can't seem to remember the moves at all.

567
00:35:00,720 --> 00:35:01,280
Sit down first, come on.

568
00:35:01,280 --> 00:35:01,760
And

569
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:04,480
I have a quiz at university tomorrow too.

570
00:35:04,480 --> 00:35:05,880
I haven't even started reading yet.

571
00:35:07,520 --> 00:35:08,880
Don't push yourself too hard, son.

572
00:35:10,600 --> 00:35:11,080
Yeah.

573
00:35:11,200 --> 00:35:12,240
When you're practicing dancing,

574
00:35:12,440 --> 00:35:14,040
could you please turn down the music a bit?

575
00:35:14,640 --> 00:35:15,760
And please,

576
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:17,760
don't stomp your feet so loudly!

577
00:35:17,760 --> 00:35:18,920
The sound gets picked up on my live stream!

578
00:35:18,920 --> 00:35:19,440
No way,

579
00:35:19,440 --> 00:35:21,720
some moves require jumping!

580
00:35:21,840 --> 00:35:23,640
It's natural that it makes a thud!

581
00:35:23,640 --> 00:35:24,560
Then jump

582
00:35:24,840 --> 00:35:25,480
lower!

583
00:35:25,480 --> 00:35:26,000
